ot of  questions there and other questions such  as does the data need to be directly  accessible will it be accessed from  on-prem and additionally speaking are  there any specific security requirements  because you may not discover them at and  when looking at the entire architecture  but when doing a deep dive on the  service you come across some of these  use cases like perhaps you have services  communicating internally and they're  using HTTPS and the other question is at  the deepest level  how are your health checks on your  services working today how do you  identify when a service is unhealthy are  you just looking at the issue to be  response code are you looking for that  plus a string how does that work in GCP  or do your health checks and GCP work  exactly the same way so these are just  an example or a subset of the questions  that we looked at for each of the  services to make sure that we recognized  what was unknown early on and identified  it so that way we can look at it so  other results of the discovery what came  out of it so after going through this  deep type discovery we actually fed the  results back into the overall arc  and adjusted her architecture a-courtin  accordingly develop criteria for  determining on a per service basis which  load balancer to use for example because  there are a few different flavors within  the platform determining how we're gonna  do dns resolution during this  split-brain period figuring out other  things such as how are we going to do  our secrets management how do how are we  going to split up our data instances for  each of the services are we gonna put  one service in a project is this  currently shared data going to be split  up into two so we went from there and  one of the most important things that we  came up with was a blueprint a blueprint  for if you are going to lift and shift  application why per this customers  requirements and their architecture and  the individual applications requirements  w